From: Active ESL <engineering@active-esl.com>
Subject: [PATCH] frt: link compiler atomic helpers

Clang emits calls to __atomic_is_lock_free for Godot core on aarch64. Add
libatomic while configuring the FRT platform so it reaches the final program
link environment; SCsub clones do not propagate libraries back to that link.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Yocto toolchain integration]

---
 platform/frt/detect.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/platform/frt/detect.py b/platform/frt/detect.py
index 0278f20..560373a 100644
--- a/platform/frt/detect.py
+++ b/platform/frt/detect.py
@@ -69,7 +69,7 @@ def configure_misc(env):
 	env.Append(CPPPATH=['#platform/frt'])
 	env.Append(CPPFLAGS=['-DUNIX_ENABLED', '-DGLES_ENABLED', '-DJOYDEV_ENABLED'])
 	env.Append(CPPFLAGS=['-DFRT_ENABLED'])
-	env.Append(LIBS=['pthread', 'z', 'dl'])
+	env.Append(LIBS=['pthread', 'z', 'dl', 'atomic'])
 	if env['use_static_cpp']:
 		env.Append(LINKFLAGS=['-static-libgcc', '-static-libstdc++'])
 	env['ENV']['PATH'] = os.getenv('PATH')
-- 
